Subject: [PATCH] dtl: bound completed staging caches on small UMA devices

Upstream ages staging buffers by fence distance without a byte budget, retaining
large upload/readback bursts on 8 GiB shared-memory systems. Use a separate
bounded cache only for the balanced profile, preserving unfinished GPU uses
and the legacy pool implementation. Track committed allocation bytes, not
application payload size. Missing capabilities select legacy behavior.

